  "raw": ", which in part says:\n\nBeginning Jan. 1, 2012, a private kindergarten annex may not utilize or provide for the services of a labor organization that is solely dedicated to and primarily engaged in lobbying for increased worker compensation or overtime.\n\nA “labor organization” is defined as a union that “gs” professionally skilled adult service workers, primarily teaching, as well as employees (even if they are self-employed, which is the international standard). It is an interesting provision — the kind that has the media and education community talking, yet proponents of the bill approved in committee say that they excluded the “Unions of Pre-Dubious Reputation.”\n\nMost of the accredited private preschools in our area are not franchised (such as Watterlee School in Los Altos or Children’s Learning House in Mountain View) and are not leased out to a chain like Early Learning Options (including Catalina’s Waldorf",
  "serialized": ", which in part says: Beginning Jan. 1, 2012, a private kindergarten annex may not utilize or provide for the services of a labor organization that is solely dedicated to and primarily engaged in lobbying for increased worker compensation or overtime. A “labor organization” is defined as a union that “gs” professionally skilled adult service workers, primarily teaching, as well as employees (even if they are self-employed, which is the international standard). It is an interesting provision — the kind that has the media and education community talking, yet proponents of the bill approved in committee say that they excluded the “Unions of Pre-Dubious Reputation.” Most of the accredited private preschools in our area are not franchised (such as Watterlee School in Los Altos or Children’s Learning House in Mountain View) and are not leased out to a chain like Early Learning Options (including Catalina’s Waldorf",
